This project is a single core Operating System built in Java. It uses Java Threads to do task switching. Throughout the project, several different task switching methods were implemented as well as 
several different devices. 
Some of these devices include a Kernel, memory, memory managament, a file system, and a virtual file system. Additionally, all of the tests that were used are in the source code so it is possible to model
tests after those. They work on a line counter where the Operating System knows which line to jump into based on the number of times that the thread was ran during the test.
